{#- One postgres container that holds the OpenTofu state of IaC-opentofu
   (`backend "pg"`). Published on postgres_port to the LAN: both the user's
   machine (apply) and Forgejo Actions jobs (plan, drift check) connect.
   scram-sha-256 (the image's pg_hba default once a password is set). The
   state itself is encrypted client-side by OpenTofu (README), so the DB
   only ever holds ciphertext.

   postgres_user: the alpine image's own user (70:70), run as directly — no
   root entrypoint, no capabilities; data_dir handed to it by :U. Needs a
   writable root (/run/postgresql), hence read_only False in podman.
   podman: spec overrides (keys: formulas/podman README).

   The DB password is required (OpenBao tofu-state/postgres); the formula fails on
   a blank or unresolved one.

   dump_dir: where formulas/backup's pre-run pg_dump goes. pillar/backup.sls
   `dumps` repeats this path, container_name, db_user and db_name — change
   them together. #}
{%- set defaults = {
    'image': 'docker.io/library/postgres',
    'tag': '18.6-alpine',
    'container_name': 'tofu-state-postgres',
    'postgres_port': 5432,
    'postgres_user': '70:70',
    'base_dir': '/opt/tofu-state',
    'data_dir': '/opt/tofu-state/postgres',
    'secrets_dir': '/opt/tofu-state/secrets',
    'dump_dir': '/opt/tofu-state/dump',
    'db_name': 'tofu',
    'db_user': 'tofu',
    'db_password': '',
    'timezone': 'Etc/UTC',
    'podman': {'read_only': False},
} %}
{%- set tofu_state = salt['pillar.get']('tofu-state:lookup', default=defaults, merge=True) %}
